{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\ns='Lemma check: for caps u_i<=d and Q=sum u-d, Q<=u_i+u_j, so corner cuts never overlap. With c_i=(Q-u_i)_+, D=Q\"'^2-sum c_i''^2, centroid g_i=[Q''^3-sum c_j''^3-3*c_i''^2*(Q-c_i)]/(3D). Thus g_i-g_j=[f(c_j)-f(c_i)]/D, f(c)=c''^2(Q-c). Since c_i+c_j<=Q, f(a)-f(b)=(a-b)[Q(a+b)-(a''^2+ab+b''^2)] has strict sign(a-b) for nondegenerate positive values. Hence g uniform iff cuts equal. This is an alternative to swap lemma.'\"'\nwith open('/work/board.md','a') as f:f.write('[sol] '+datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()+' '+s+'\\\\n')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
