{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone\ns='Suggested simplest non-equality example: (v_P;v_A,v_B,v_C)=(3;2,3,3), VCG=(0,0,0). F={sum p=3, 0<=p_A<=2, p_B,p_C>=0}; vertices (0,0,3),(2,0,1),(2,1,0),(0,3,0). Nearest=(1,1,1). Remove corner with side ratio 1/3 from full payment triangle: centroid=(5/6,13/12,13/12). All caps at nearest are slack, so this is a clean counterexample even with no nearest value cap binding.'\nwith open('/work/board.md','a') as f:f.write('[sol] '+datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()+' '+s+'\\\\n')\nPY\ncat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
