egment and equality always. Please check independently; I can write final proof unless another agent already doing so.\n[argon] 2026-10-22T20:43:29Z Starting analysis of core face F, VCG-nearest point, and polygon centroid. Running symbolic/numerical classification across parameter regimes.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:49Z AGREED opus owns writing answer.md. Your equal-cut characterization is equivalent to my union above: all cuts zero iff Q<=min u; positive equal cuts iff all u equal. I will supply/check strict centroid-order lemma and examples, then audit your draft.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:43:44.600463+00:00 Lemma check: for caps u_i<=d and Q=sum u-d, Q<=u_i+u_j, so corner cuts never overlap. With c_i=(Q-u_i)_+, D=Q^2-sum c_i^2, centroid g_i=[Q^3-sum c_j^3-3*c_i^2*(Q-c_i)]/(3D). Thus g_i-g_j=[f(c_j)-f(c_i)]/D, f(c)=c^2(Q-c). Since c_i+c_j<=Q, f(a)-f(b)=(a-b)[Q(a+b)-(a^2+ab+b^2)] has strict sign(a-b) for nondegenerate positive values. Hence g uniform iff cuts equal. This is an alternative to swap lemma.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:43:58.662650+00:00 Suggested simplest non-equality example: (v_P;v_A,v_B,v_C)=(3;2,3,3), VCG=(0,0,0). F={sum p=3, 0<=p_A<=2, p_B,p_C>=0}; vertices (0,0,3),(2,0,1),(2,1,0),(0,3,0). Nearest=(1,1,1). Remove corner with side ratio 1/3 from full payment triangle: centroid=(5/6,13/12,13/12). All caps at nearest are slack, so this is a clean counterexample even with no nearest value cap binding.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /work/check_sol.py <<'PY'\nfrom itertools import product, combinations\nfrom math import atan2\nfrom random import Random\n\ndef centroid(v,P):\n    pts=[]\n    for i,j in combinations(range(3),2):\n        k=3-i-j\n        for a,b in product((0,1),repeat=2):\n            x=[0.,0.,0.]; x[i]=a*v[i]; x[j]=b*v[j]; x[k]=P-x[i]-x[j]\n            if -1e-10<=x[k]<=v[k]+1e-10: pts.append(tuple(x))\n    pts=list(set(pts)); m=[sum(x[i] for x in pts)/len(pts) for i in range(3)]\n    pts.sort(key=lambda x:atan2(x[1]-m[1],x[0]-m[0])); cross=[]\n    for x,y in zip(pts,pts[1:]+pts[:1]):cross.append(x[0]*y[1]-y[0]*x[1])\n    a=sum(cross)\n    if abs(a)<1e-10:return m\n    out=[sum((x[i]+y[i])*c for x,y,c in zip(pts,pts[1:]+pts[:1],cross))/(3*a) for i in range(2)]\n    return out+[P-sum(out)]\ndef nearest(v,P):\n    d=sum(v)-P;l=[max(0,x-d) for x in v]\n    lo=0.;hi=max(v)\n    for _ in range(80):\n        t=(lo+hi)/2\n        if sum(min(x,z+t) for x,z in zip(v,l))>P:hi=t\n        else:lo=t\n    return [min(x,z+(lo+hi)/2) for x,z in zip(v,l)]\n\nr=Random(20261022);n=0\nfor v in product(range(1,9),repeat=3):\n for P in range(1,sum(v)):\n    c=centroid(v,P); p=nearest(v,P)\n    equal=max(abs(x-y) for x,y in zip(c,p))<1e-8\n    expect=(P<=min(v) or sum(v)-P<=min(v) or len(set(v))==1)\n    assert equal==expect,(v,P,c,p,expect)\n    n+=1\nprint('Exhaustive independent polygon and projection check passed:',n,'positive integer instances')\nprint('Worked example:',centroid((2,3,3),3),nearest((2,3,3),3))\nPY\npython /work/check_sol.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /work/check_sol.py <<'PY'\nfrom itertools import product, combinations\nfrom math import atan2\nfrom random import Random\n\ndef centroid(v,P):\n    pts=[]\n    for i,j in combinations(range(3),2):\n        k=3-i-j\n        for a,b in product((0,1),repeat=2):\n            x=[0.,0.,0.]; x[i]=a*v[i]; x[j]=b*v[j]; x[k]=P-x[i]-x[j]\n            if -1e-10<=x[k]<=v[k]+1e-10: pts.append(tuple(x))\n    pts=list(set(pts)); m=[sum(x[i] for x in pts)/len(pts) for i in range(3)]\n    pts.sort(key=lambda x:atan2(x[1]-m[1],x[0]-m[0])); cross=[]\n    for x,y in zip(pts,pts[1:]+pts[:1]):cross.append(x[0]*y[1]-y[0]*x[1])\n    a=sum(cross)\n    if abs(a)<1e-10:return m\n    out=[sum((x[i]+y[i])*c for x,y,c in zip(pts,pts[1:]+pts[:1],cross))/(3*a) for i in range(2)]\n    return out+[P-sum(out)]\ndef nearest(v,P):\n    d=sum(v)-P;l=[max(0,x-d) for x in v]\n    lo=0.;hi=max(v)\n    for _ in range(80):\n        t=(lo+hi)/2\n        if sum(min(x,z+t) for x,z in zip(v,l))>P:hi=t\n        else:lo=t\n    return [min(x,z+(lo+hi)/2) for x,z in zip(v,l)]\n\nr=Random(20261022);n=0\nfor v in product(range(1,9),repeat=3):\n for P in range(1,sum(v)):\n    c=centroid(v,P); p=nearest(v,P)\n    equal=max(abs(x-y) for x,y in zip(c,p))<1e-8\n    expect=(P<=min(v) or sum(v)-P<=min(v) or len(set(v))==1)\n    assert equal==expect,(v,P,c,p,expect)\n    n+=1\nprint('Exhaustive independent polygon and projection check passed:',n,'positive integer instances')\nprint('Worked example:',centroid((2,3,3),3),nearest((2,3,3),3))\nPY\npython /work/check_sol.py\"","aggregated_output":"Exhaustive independent polygon and projection check passed: 6400 positive integer instances\nWorked example: [0.8333333333333334, 1.0833333333333333, 1.0833333333333335] [1.0, 1.0, 1.0]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone\nwith open('/work/board.md','a') as f:f.write('[sol] '+datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()+' Independent exhaustive polygon-vertex centroid and binary-search projection check PASSED all 6,400 positive integer instances v_i in 1..8, 0<P<sum v. Verified simple union condition exactly, and example centroid (5/6,13/12,13/12). Check script /work/check_sol.py.\\\\n')\nPY\ncat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone\nwith open('/work/board.md','a') as f:f.write('[sol] '+datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()+' Independent exhaustive polygon-vertex centroid and binary-search projection check PASSED all 6,400 positive integer instances v_i in 1..8, 0<P<sum v. Verified simple union condition exactly, and example centroid (5/6,13/12,13/12). Check script /work/check_sol.py.\\\\n')\nPY\ncat /work/board.md\"","aggregated_output":"[sol] 2026-10-22T00:00Z Reading problem; I will derive a geometric characterization and coordinate final content here.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:43Z Derived: with d=sum(v_i)-v_P>0, F={0<=p_i<=v_i, sum p_i=v_P}. Utilities x_i=v_i-p_i give capped simplex sum x_i=d. VCG utility u_i=min(v_i,d); nearest is x_i=max(0,u_i-t) with sum=d. I am seeking simplified equality classification; inclusion-exclusion centroid gives fallback exact algebraic condition. Other agents: please independently investigate classification/proof or examples; indicate who will write answer.md.\n[opus] 20:43 Working: reduce to q=p-pVCG, F={sum q=m, 0<=q_i<=u_i}, u_i=min(v_i,d), d=sum v - v_P; claim no corner-cut overlaps; centroid=projection iff cut sizes c_i=max(0,m-u_i) all equal. Verifying numerically now, will draft answer.md.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:48Z BREAKTHROUGH candidate full condition (positive item values): equality iff P<=min(v_i) OR d=V-P<=min(v_i) OR all three v_i equal. Proof: translate y=p-l (VCG), caps u_i=min(v_i,d), sum Q=sum u-d. Nearest centroid equality forces centroid y uniform (centroid strictly inside caps); uniform centroid of capped simplex iff all caps equal OR Q<=min caps, by pairwise swapping showing centroid coordinate strictly increases with any differing active cap. Zero item value reduces to segment and equality always. Please check independently; I can write final proof unless another agent already doing so.\n[argon] 2026-10-22T20:43:29Z Starting analysis of core face F, VCG-nearest point, and polygon centroid. Running symbolic/numerical classification across parameter regimes.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:49Z AGREED opus owns writing answer.md. Your equal-cut characterization is equivalent to my union above: all cuts zero iff Q<=min u; positive equal cuts iff all u equal. I will supply/check strict centroid-order lemma and examples, then audit your draft.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:43:44.600463+00:00 Lemma check: for caps u_i<=d and Q=sum u-d, Q<=u_i+u_j, so corner cuts never overlap. With c_i=(Q-u_i)_+, D=Q^2-sum c_i^2, centroid g_i=[Q^3-sum c_j^3-3*c_i^2*(Q-c_i)]/(3D). Thus g_i-g_j=[f(c_j)-f(c_i)]/D, f(c)=c^2(Q-c). Since c_i+c_j<=Q, f(a)-f(b)=(a-b)[Q(a+b)-(a^2+ab+b^2)] has strict sign(a-b) for nondegenerate positive values. Hence g uniform iff cuts equal. This is an alternative to swap lemma.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:43:58.662650+00:00 Suggested simplest non-equality example: (v_P;v_A,v_B,v_C)=(3;2,3,3), VCG=(0,0,0). F={sum p=3, 0<=p_A<=2, p_B,p_C>=0}; vertices (0,0,3),(2,0,1),(2,1,0),(0,3,0). Nearest=(1,1,1). Remove corner with side ratio 1/3 from full payment triangle: centroid=(5/6,13/12,13/12). All caps at nearest are slack, so this is a clean counterexample even with no nearest value cap binding.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:44:16.289616+00:00 Independent exhaustive polygon-vertex centroid and binary-search projection check PASSED all 6,400 positive integer instances v_i in 1..8, 0<P<sum v. Verified simple union condition exactly, and example centroid (5/6,13/12,13/12). Check script /work/check_sol.py.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nfrom datetime import datetime,timezone\ns='Degenerate proof for final: if v_C=0 and a=v_A,b=v_B, let alpha=max(0,P-b), beta=min(a,P). F={(t,P-t,0):alpha<=t<=beta}; VCG=(alpha,P-beta,0). Distance squared=(t-alpha)\"'^2+(beta-t)''^2, uniquely minimized at t=(alpha+beta)/2, the segment centroid. If <=1 positive winner, F is a point. Thus min v_i=0 gives equality always; specify centroid relative to affine hull. For positive vi, P=0 also point.'\"'\nwith open('/work/board.md','a') as f:f.write('[sol] '+datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()+' '+s+'\\\\n')\nPY\nls /work/answer.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
