{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'tail -n 10 /work/board.md; stat /work/answer.md'","aggregated_output":"[sol] 2026-10-22T20:48Z BREAKTHROUGH candidate full condition (positive item values): equality iff P<=min(v_i) OR d=V-P<=min(v_i) OR all three v_i equal. Proof: translate y=p-l (VCG), caps u_i=min(v_i,d), sum Q=sum u-d. Nearest centroid equality forces centroid y uniform (centroid strictly inside caps); uniform centroid of capped simplex iff all caps equal OR Q<=min caps, by pairwise swapping showing centroid coordinate strictly increases with any differing active cap. Zero item value reduces to segment and equality always. Please check independently; I can write final proof unless another agent already doing so.\n[argon] 2026-10-22T20:43:29Z Starting analysis of core face F, VCG-nearest point, and polygon centroid. Running symbolic/numerical classification across parameter regimes.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:49Z AGREED opus owns writing answer.md. Your equal-cut characterization is equivalent to my union above: all cuts zero iff Q<=min u; positive equal cuts iff all u equal. I will supply/check strict centroid-order lemma and examples, then audit your draft.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:43:44.600463+00:00 Lemma check: for caps u_i<=d and Q=sum u-d, Q<=u_i+u_j, so corner cuts never overlap. With c_i=(Q-u_i)_+, D=Q^2-sum c_i^2, centroid g_i=[Q^3-sum c_j^3-3*c_i^2*(Q-c_i)]/(3D). Thus g_i-g_j=[f(c_j)-f(c_i)]/D, f(c)=c^2(Q-c). Since c_i+c_j<=Q, f(a)-f(b)=(a-b)[Q(a+b)-(a^2+ab+b^2)] has strict sign(a-b) for nondegenerate positive values. Hence g uniform iff cuts equal. This is an alternative to swap lemma.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:43:58.662650+00:00 Suggested simplest non-equality example: (v_P;v_A,v_B,v_C)=(3;2,3,3), VCG=(0,0,0). F={sum p=3, 0<=p_A<=2, p_B,p_C>=0}; vertices (0,0,3),(2,0,1),(2,1,0),(0,3,0). Nearest=(1,1,1). Remove corner with side ratio 1/3 from full payment triangle: centroid=(5/6,13/12,13/12). All caps at nearest are slack, so this is a clean counterexample even with no nearest value cap binding.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:44:16.289616+00:00 Independent exhaustive polygon-vertex centroid and binary-search projection check PASSED all 6,400 positive integer instances v_i in 1..8, 0<P<sum v. Verified simple union condition exactly, and example centroid (5/6,13/12,13/12). Check script /work/check_sol.py.\n[opus] 20:44 Drafted /work/answer.md (condition: v_P<=min v_i OR d<=min v_i OR v_A=v_B=v_C; proof + examples). sol/argon please audit; I'll clean examples section.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:44:40.422084+00:00 Degenerate proof for final: if v_C=0 and a=v_A,b=v_B, let alpha=max(0,P-b), beta=min(a,P). F={(t,P-t,0):alpha<=t<=beta}; VCG=(alpha,P-beta,0). Distance squared=(t-alpha)^2+(beta-t)^2, uniquely minimized at t=(alpha+beta)/2, the segment centroid. If <=1 positive winner, F is a point. Thus min v_i=0 gives equality always; specify centroid relative to affine hull. For positive vi, P=0 also point.\n[opus] 20:44 answer.md updated incl. sol's (3;2,3,3) example; all examples numerically verified. Will mark FINAL in ~2 min unless objections.\n[sol] 2026-10-22T20:45:06.889848+00:00 AUDIT corrections needed in draft: (1) example (10;8,4,2) F is quadrilateral, not pentagon; (6,2,2) is interior of top edge, delete it. Centroid numbers are correct. (2) case1 parenthesis cap may touch a vertex at equality; say no corner is cut off. case2 every VCG price positive false at d=min v: some zero. (3) Step5 c_i+c_j<=2m-u_i-u_j only valid when both cuts positive; if one zero use c_i+c_j<m since positive vi => c_i<m. (4) sufficiency equal caps gives u>m/3 STRICT because sumu-m=d>0. (5) Please include zero-value/zero-P cases, since problem allows lower-dimensional F. Suggested add simple trapezoid non-equality example (3;2,3,3) from earlier board.\n  File: /work/answer.md\n  Size: 5980      \tBlocks: 16         IO Block: 4096   regular file\nDevice: 0,159\tInode: 10908767779  Links: 1\nAccess: (0644/-rw-r--r--)  Uid: ( 1000/   agent)   Gid: ( 1000/   agent)\nAccess: 2026-10-22 20:44:38.898835237 +0000\nModify: 2026-10-22 20:44:45.575820248 +0000\nChange: 2026-10-22 20:44:45.575820248 +0000\n Birth: 2026-10-22 20:44:31.809851145 +0000\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
